##### SUMMARY
<!--- Explain the problem briefly -->
With apply_immeditely set to 'yes':
If I try and use the module to modify an instance from multi_zone: no to multi_zone: yes, it works.
BUT, if I try and use the module to modify an instance from multi_zone: yes to multi_zone: no, it says "changed" but no action is triggered. Again, apply_immediately is set to 'yes'.
##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE
<!---
For bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case.
For new features, show how the feature would be used.
-->
Create an RDS instance with multi_zone set to `no`.
Write an ansible play to modify said instance multi_zone to `yes`.
eg:
```
- name: modify db instance
      rds:
        command: modify
        region: us-west-2
        instance_name: test-db
        multi_zone: yes
        apply_immediately: yes
        wait: yes
```
Run play and confirm that mutli_az has been changed from `no` to `yes`. 👍 
Now change play to modify instance from multi_zone `yes` to multi_zone `no`
eg
```
- name: modify db instance
      rds:
        command: modify
        region: us-west-2
        instance_name: test-db
        multi_zone: no
        apply_immediately: yes
        wait: yes
```
Run the play and confirm that play does not throw and error of any kind, but appears to work.
Check the RDS instance and you will see that no modification has been triggered, and multi_az remains set to `yes`. 👎 

